{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - IDP - Okta Identity Provider Client Secret Read",
	"Description": "Someone read the client secret of a configured identity provider. Reading it is not normal operations after setup; the secret lets the holder impersonate the Okta side of that federation.\n\nEvent type: system.idp.lifecycle.read_client_secret\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "ed2a20ed-1f5e-5e79-a1e4-5b863265c2e7",
